    "result": "Perfect! The feature is fully implemented and working correctly. Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the one-line summary feature for frai-gate. Here's what was added:\n\n### 1. **`renderSummary()` function** (`src/gate/report.ts`)\n   - Exports a new function that returns a single-line summary: `<VERDICT> <answered>/7`\n   - Appends blocked check IDs when there are failures: `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency`\n   - Special case: If gate section is missing, returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure`\n   - Check IDs are ordered according to `GATE_CHECKS` definition\n\n### 2. **`--summary` CLI flag** (`src/cli.ts`)\n   - Added to `frai-gate check` command\n   - Prints only the summary line to stdout\n   - Maintains correct exit codes (1 for BLOCK, 0 for PASS/WARN)\n   - Respects flag priority: `--json` takes precedence if both are specified\n\n### 3. **Documentation & Tests**\n   - Updated HELP text with `--summary` flag documentation and usage example\n   - Created comprehensive test suite (`report.test.ts`) with 7 test cases covering:\n     - All checks answered (PASS)\n     - Warnings only (WARN)\n     - Missing gate section (structure finding)\n     - Single and multiple blocked checks\n     - Proper ordering of check IDs\n   - All 18 tests pass \u2705\n\n### 4. **Build & Export**\n   - Added `renderSummary` to package exports in `src/index.ts`\n   - TypeScript build successful with no errors\n   - Ready for use as a library export\n\nThe feature is tested, building successfully, and fully functional. All requirements have been met! \ud83d\ude80",
